   "id": "causal-estimation",
   "label": "Causal estimates of each change: interrupted series and matched periods",
   "maturity": "surfaced",
   "evidence": [
    {
     "gate": "engine"
    }
   ],
   "note": "each Response's before/after estimate is reported beside an interrupted series (level and rate against the old trend projected to the change, standard errors widened for day-to-day carry-over) and a matched-periods estimate (the same comparison at dates in the person's own record with no change: same weekday and phase, a similar starting trend, Student's t for few periods); a person's deliberate changes, pooled per unit, are an identification strategy of their own. Observational: it rules out drift and regression to the mean, not a cause that arrived with the change",
   "source": "segmented regression of interrupted time series (Wagner et al. 2002, J Clin Pharm Ther); the AR(1) variance factor for a trend regressor; caliper matching (Austin 2011, Pharm Stat)",
